{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"533","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Correcting Mistakes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Analyzing the mistakes people make while typing search queries is a complex and an interesting work. As there is no guaranteed way to determine what the user originally meant by typing some query, we have to use different sorts of heuristics."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarp needed to write a code that could, given two words, check whether they could have been obtained from the same word as a result of typos. Polycarpus suggested that the most common typo is skipping exactly one letter as you type a word."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Implement a program that can, given two distinct words "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the same length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" determine how many words "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" are there with such property that you can transform "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" into both "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" by deleting exactly one character. Words "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" consist of lowercase English letters. Word "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" also should consist of lowercase English letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the length of words "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains word "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains word "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Words "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" consist of lowercase English letters. It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" are distinct words."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the number of distinct words "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" that can be transformed to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" due to a typo."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7\nreading\ntrading\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\nsweet\nsheep\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\ntoy\ntry\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample test the two given words could be obtained only from word \""},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"r"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"e"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"ading"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","t